+# Flight 93 telephone summary at the April 11 trial session
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1. The archived Volume XVII-A transcript records the prosecutor offering **P200055** on April 11, 2006, citing stipulation 36. Defense counsel stated there was no objection, the court received the exhibit, and the prosecutor asked to put it on the screen. Later the witness said he created a call chart after reviewing the calls. This gives an exact trial-session locator and identifies a witness who described how the chart was compiled. [Transcript, printed pp. 3450 and 3461–3463, PDF pp. 65 and 76–78](https://web.archive.org/web/20100114150613/http://911myths.com/images/f/f8/Moussaoui_Trial_Transcript_April_11_2006.pdf#page=65)
+
+## Source and scope
+
+- The **94-page archived transcript** is a reporter transcript reproduced by a third-party host. Its cover gives April 11, 2006 at 1:30 p.m. and Volume XVII-A. Printed p. 3478, lines 16–22, contains a reporter certification statement. The court docket separately lists **1823** as a redacted transcript and **1833** as a transcript for that same session. Their linked public notices were inspected in the preceding study. The available copy's relationship to those two versions remains unverified. [Court docket, lines 106 and 122](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/DocketSheet1.html) · [Transcript, PDF p. 93](https://web.archive.org/web/20100114150613/http://911myths.com/images/f/f8/Moussaoui_Trial_Transcript_April_11_2006.pdf#page=93)
+- The separate **75-page ST00001 Part A scan** was recovered from an archived court URL. Its face has a March 1, 2006 filing stamp and the printed exhibit label **ST00001** with a handwritten mark beside it. The archived filename is **ST00001A.pdf**. The live court listing identifies ST00001 and links Part A and Part B. The court docket separately describes the March 1 Part One filing, item **1632**, as sealed. Byte identity to the filed docket version remains unverified. [Archived Part A, cover](https://web.archive.org/web/20190207163520/http://www.vaed.uscourts.gov/notablecases/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00001A.pdf#page=1) · [Court exhibit listing, lines 5–8](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00001.html) · [March 1 docket entries 1632–1639](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/DocketSheet2.html)
+- The earlier recovered **ST00004**, ¶36, specifies authenticity of the documents supporting the Flight 93 summary. It does not itemize them. The court site lists P200055 as a Flash presentation that also covers the other three flights. The package and any native documents used in its preparation were outside this review. The transcript's exhibit reception and witness account are separate from the authenticity wording in the stipulation. [ST00004, printed p. 11](https://web.archive.org/web/20210130105845/https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00004.pdf#page=11) · [P200055 court entry, lines 5–8](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200055.html)
+
+## Observations and open comparisons
+
+| Question | March 1 stipulated narrative | April 11 witness account | Status and discriminating record |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **9:32 United maintenance call** | ST00001 Part A ¶4(h), printed and PDF p. 10, reports three people **“with knives and bombs”**. | Volume XVII-A p. 3476, lines 14–18, describes a **9:32**, **95-second** call from **34 ABC** and says **“they had a bomb”**. | The accounts differ in number and both attribute the information to a call report. The apparent match uses time and destination. Obtain a native call key and contemporaneous maintenance note or audio to test whether the accounts refer to the same call and what was said. |
+| **Burnett call types** | Part A ¶4(e), printed and PDF p. 9, describes several calls beginning at **9:30 a.m.** from rows **24 and 25**. | P. 3473, lines 2–6, attributes **three** calls from **24 A, B, and C and 25 A, B, and C** to Airfone records and separately reports his wife's account of possible additional cell calls. P. 3477, lines 13–16, gives **35 airphone calls and two cellular phone calls** as the total the witness was able to determine for the chart. | The reported possibility of other cellular calls and the chart total both stand. The first account's selected row descriptions and the later testimony overlap. Determine which calls or attempts the chart counted using caller-side records, recipient-leg records and the worksheet linking them. |
+| **Beamer routing** | Part A ¶4(o), printed and PDF p. 11, describes a **9:43 a.m.** attempt from row **32** routed to a GTE operator. | P. 3468, lines 15–25, describes **four** calls from **32 DEF**, three that did not connect, the fourth redirected to the GTE operator, and a subsequent supervisor transfer. P. 3469, lines 1–12, separately describes the supervisor conversation. | The number of attempts and the connection/transfer are distinct events. The stipulation describes one routed attempt and gives no full attempt count in ¶4(o). An operator bridge record or keyed switch/recipient record could test the relationship between these accounts. |
+
+[Part A, pp. 9–11](https://web.archive.org/web/20190207163520/http://www.vaed.uscourts.gov/notablecases/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00001A.pdf#page=9) · [Volume XVII-A, pp. 3468–3477](https://web.archive.org/web/20100114150613/http://911myths.com/images/f/f8/Moussaoui_Trial_Transcript_April_11_2006.pdf#page=83)
+
+The trial witness described seat and row identification from equipment records at pp. 3462–3463, lines 13–25 and 1–4. The chart discussion distinguishes unsuccessful attempts from conversations at pp. 3468 and 3476. The statement at p. 3477, lines 13–16, is the witness's count of what he determined. The court asked whether the defense had questions and counsel said it had none, pp. 3477, lines 17–23. The sources establish how the summary was presented. They leave open which source records were joined and whether the count exhausts all attempts. The separate docket versions and the varying call descriptions stay open. [Transcript, pp. 3462–3463 and 3477](https://web.archive.org/web/20100114150613/http://911myths.com/images/f/f8/Moussaoui_Trial_Transcript_April_11_2006.pdf#page=77)
+
